{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":735,"cacheRead":10644,"cacheWrite":1288,"reasoning":17,"totalTokens":12669,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.036750000000000005,"cacheRead":0.010643999999999999,"cacheWrite":0.0161,"total":0.063514}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"All done. Summary:\n\n**Root cause** (two coupled bugs in `event-projector.mjs`):\n1. A single module-wide `pending` promise chained *all* trades' events. After any rejection, the rejected promise stayed as the chain tail, so every later `project` call rejected too — a globally poisoned queue that also blocked unrelated trades behind one slow persistence call.\n2. `states.set(next)` ran *before* `await applyToStore(...)`, so state committed even when persistence rejected. There was also no validation of ordering, first-event rules, terminality, payload validity, or event types, and inputs were held by reference.\n\n**Repair**:\n- Per-trade queue map (`Map<tradeId, Promise>`) — serial per trade, concurrent across trades; queue tails swallow rejections so one failure never blocks later events.\n- Commit `states.set` only after `applyToStore` resolves.\n- Full validation: `TypeError` for malformed events/unsupported types/invalid payloads; first event must be `CREATED` v1 with positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`; later events require exactly `version + 1`; duplicate/stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting; `CANCELLED` is terminal; `AMENDED` fields validated.\n- Defensive `structuredClone` on intake events, callback state, returned states, and snapshots.\n\n**Tests added** (`student-tests.mjs`, 6 tests): cross-trade concurrency (blocked trade doesn't stall another), duplicate/stale no-op behavior, gap/invalid-first rejection without poisoning, cancelled-is-terminal, `TypeError` on malformed events/payloads, and immutability of all exposed values.\n\n**Test result**:\n```\nℹ tests 8   (2 committed + 6 student)\nℹ pass 8\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n**Remaining risk** (documented in `INCIDENT.md`): store-write vs. in-memory commit isn't atomic across a crash; no store reconciliation/replay; `states`/`queues` maps grow unbounded with trade cardinality.\n\nOnly the three permitted fixture files were changed."}}
