{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Diagnose and repair the event projector\n\nThe synthetic trade event projector in\n`benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs` fails after a\ntemporary persistence rejection and also blocks unrelated trades behind one\nglobal queue.\n\nRepair it, replace `student-tests.mjs` with at least four meaningful regression\ntests, and complete `INCIDENT.md`.\n\n## Required behavior\n\n- `createEventProjector(applyToStore)` returns `project(event)` and\n  `getSnapshot(tradeId)`.\n- Events for one trade are applied serially in call order. Different trades\n  must be able to make progress concurrently.\n- The first accepted event is `CREATED` at version 1. Later accepted events use\n  exactly the current version plus one.\n- Duplicate or stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting.\n- A version gap or an invalid first event rejects without changing state.\n- A `CANCELLED` trade is terminal and rejects a later new version.\n- State commits only after `applyToStore` succeeds. A rejection must not poison\n  later work for that trade or another trade.\n- `CREATED` requires positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`.\n  `AMENDED` may replace either field but must leave a valid complete state.\n- Supported types are `CREATED`, `AMENDED`, and `CANCELLED`; malformed events\n  reject with `TypeError`.\n- Inputs, callback values, returned states, and snapshots must not expose\n  mutable internal state.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Change only `event-projector.mjs`, `student-tests.mjs`, and `INCIDENT.md` in\n  this fixture.\n- Do not edit the committed test, task definitions, harness files, or generated\n  evidence.\n- Do not install dependencies, use the network, add sleeps or retry loops,\n  commit, or start a service.\n- Run:\n  `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs`\n\nThe final response must state the root cause, repair, tests added, visible test\nresult, and remaining risk.\n"}],"timestamp":1787544628267},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01KcZqiXb6EmiYXEMLb4RC2X","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JyNmbreeoCvrbuz4HyCnFf","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JJqRpLWSeFq4pcL1MtY5eF","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_018RtPXn4SKMSd87yP3JwgHf","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":273,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":4512,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":4786,"cost":{"input":0.00001,"output":0.01365,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0564,"total":0.07006}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787544628303,"responseId":"gen-1787544628-tSVgB8o6jQM5XjDSza6E","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01KcZqiXb6EmiYXEMLb4RC2X","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"function copyState(state) {\n  return state ? structuredClone(state) : null;\n}\n\nfunction reduceEvent(previous, event) {\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n    return {\n      tradeId: event.tradeId,\n      version: event.version,\n      status: \"active\",\n      notional: event.payload.notional,\n      owner: event.payload.owner,\n    };\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    return { ...previous, ...event.payload, version: event.version };\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"CANCELLED\") {\n    return { ...previous, version: event.version, status: \"cancelled\" };\n  }\n  throw new TypeError(`unsupported event type: ${event.type}`);\n}\n\nexport function createEventProjector(applyToStore) {\n  if (typeof applyToStore !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"applyToStore must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  const states = new Map();\n  let pending = Promise.resolve();\n\n  async function project(event) {\n    pending = pending.then(async () => {\n      const next = reduceEvent(states.get(event.tradeId), event);\n      states.set(event.tradeId, next);\n      await applyToStore(event.tradeId, copyState(next), structuredClone(event));\n      return copyState(next);\n    });\n    return pending;\n  }\n\n  function getSnapshot(tradeId) {\n    return copyState(states.get(tradeId));\n  }\n\n  return { project, getSnapshot };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787544631732},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JyNmbreeoCvrbuz4HyCnFf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Replace this placeholder with at least four meaningful node:test cases.\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\ntest(\"replace this placeholder with projector regression tests\", () => {\n  assert.fail(\"Add at least four meaningful tests\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787544631732},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JJqRpLWSeFq4pcL1MtY5eF","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Event projector incident\n\nStatus: investigation pending\n\n## Impact\n\nComplete after diagnosing the fixture.\n\n## Root cause\n\nComplete after diagnosing the fixture.\n\n## Fix\n\nComplete after implementing the repair.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\nComplete after adding tests.\n\n## Remaining risk\n\nComplete after verification.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787544631732},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_018RtPXn4SKMSd87yP3JwgHf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { createEventProjector } from \"./event-projector.mjs\";\n\nconst created = (tradeId = \"trade-1\") => ({\n  tradeId,\n  version: 1,\n  type: \"CREATED\",\n  payload: { notional: 100, owner: \"desk-a\" },\n});\n\ntest(\"serializes concurrent events for one trade\", async () => {\n  const persisted = [];\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async (_tradeId, state) => {\n    await Promise.resolve();\n    persisted.push(state.version);\n  });\n\n  const first = projector.project(created());\n  const second = projector.project({\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 2,\n    type: \"AMENDED\",\n    payload: { notional: 125 },\n  });\n\n  await Promise.all([first, second]);\n  assert.deepEqual(persisted, [1, 2]);\n  assert.deepEqual(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\"), {\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 2,\n    status: \"active\",\n    notional: 125,\n    owner: \"desk-a\",\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"a persistence rejection does not commit state or poison later work\", async () => {\n  let fail = true;\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async () => {\n    if (fail) {\n      fail = false;\n      throw new Error(\"temporary store failure\");\n    }\n  });\n\n  await assert.rejects(projector.project(created()), /temporary store failure/);\n  assert.equal(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\"), null);\n  assert.equal((await projector.project(created())).version, 1);\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787544631732},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm redesigning the projector to use a per-trade queue with validation before committing, only persisting after applyToStore succeeds, and deep-copying inputs. I need to define strict validation rules—rejecting malformed events with TypeError, enforcing version sequencing where the first event must be CREATED at version 1, duplicates or stale versions return the current snapshot unchanged, and version gaps trigger a rejection.\n\nI'm also working out field-level rules: CANCELLED is terminal, CREATED requires a positive finite notional and non-empty owner, AMENDED can update either field but must leave the state valid, and I'm cloning both the incoming event and the state passed to callbacks to preserve immutability.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01T4WebwNKfNYmb1ZhQDZa2W","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs","content":"const SUPPORTED_TYPES = new Set([\"CREATED\", \"AMENDED\", \"CANCELLED\"]);\n\nfunction copyState(state) {\n  return state ? structuredClone(state) : null;\n}\n\nfunction isNonEmptyString(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"string\" && value.length > 0;\n}\n\nfunction isValidNotional(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(value) && value > 0;\n}\n\nfunction validateEventShape(event) {\n  if (event === null || typeof event !== \"object\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event must be an object\");\n  }\n  if (!isNonEmptyString(event.tradeId)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event.tradeId must be a non-empty string\");\n  }\n  if (!Number.isInteger(event.version) || event.version < 1) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event.version must be a positive integer\");\n  }\n  if (!SUPPORTED_TYPES.has(event.type)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`unsupported event type: ${String(event.type)}`);\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\" || event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    if (event.payload === null || typeof event.payload !== \"object\") {\n      throw new TypeError(`event.payload must be an object for ${event.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction reduceEvent(previous, event) {\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n    if (previous !== undefined) {\n      throw new Error(`trade ${event.tradeId} already exists`);\n    }\n    if (event.version !== 1) {\n      throw new Error(\"first event must be CREATED at version 1\");\n    }\n    if (!isValidNotional(event.payload.notional)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"CREATED requires a positive finite notional\");\n    }\n    if (!isNonEmptyString(event.payload.owner)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"CREATED requires a non-empty owner\");\n    }\n    return {\n      tradeId: event.tradeId,\n      version: event.version,\n      status: \"active\",\n      notional: event.payload.notional,\n      owner: event.payload.owner,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (previous === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(\"first event must be CREATED at version 1\");\n  }\n  if (previous.status === \"cancelled\") {\n    throw new Error(`trade ${event.tradeId} is cancelled and terminal`);\n  }\n  if (event.version !== previous.version + 1) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `version gap for trade ${event.tradeId}: expected ${previous.version + 1}, got ${event.version}`,\n    );\n  }\n\n  if (event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    const next = { ...previous, version: event.version };\n    if (\"notional\" in event.payload) {\n      if (!isValidNotional(event.payload.notional)) {\n        throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED notional must be positive and finite\");\n      }\n      next.notional = event.payload.notional;\n    }\n    if (\"owner\" in event.payload) {\n      if (!isNonEmptyString(event.payload.owner)) {\n        throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED owner must be a non-empty string\");\n      }\n      next.owner = event.payload.owner;\n    }\n    return next;\n  }\n\n  // CANCELLED\n  return { ...previous, version: event.version, status: \"cancelled\" };\n}\n\nexport function createEventProjector(applyToStore) {\n  if (typeof applyToStore !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"applyToStore must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  const states = new Map();\n  const queues = new Map();\n\n  async function apply(event) {\n    const previous = states.get(event.tradeId);\n\n    // Duplicate or stale version: return current snapshot, no persistence.\n    if (previous !== undefined && event.version <= previous.version) {\n      return copyState(previous);\n    }\n\n    const next = reduceEvent(previous, event);\n\n    // Commit only after successful persistence.\n    await applyToStore(event.tradeId, copyState(next), structuredClone(event));\n    states.set(event.tradeId, next);\n    return copyState(next);\n  }\n\n  function project(event) {\n    // Validate synchronously against the caller's object, then take a\n    // defensive copy so later caller mutation cannot affect processing.\n    validateEventShape(event);\n    const frozenEvent = structuredClone(event);\n\n    const tail = queues.get(frozenEvent.tradeId) ?? Promise.resolve();\n    const run = tail.then(\n      () => apply(frozenEvent),\n      () => apply(frozenEvent),\n    );\n    // Keep the per-trade queue alive even when this event rejects.\n    queues.set(\n      frozenEvent.tradeId,\n      run.then(\n        () => undefined,\n        () => undefined,\n      ),\n    );\n    return run;\n  }\n\n  function getSnapshot(tradeId) {\n    return copyState(states.get(tradeId));\n  }\n\n  return { project, getSnapshot };\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":2048,"cacheRead":4512,"cacheWrite":1588,"reasoning":299,"totalTokens":8150,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.1024,"cacheRead":0.0045119999999999995,"cacheWrite":0.01985,"total":0.126782}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787544631733,"responseId":"gen-1787544631-FgNuvc9byheZUForAmnJ","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01T4WebwNKfNYmb1ZhQDZa2W","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 4358 bytes to benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787544651556},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should make project() reject with a rejected promise rather than throw synchronously for malformed events, matching how the committed test handles persistence failures with assert.rejects. I'll wrap the validation logic so failures consistently return rejected promises.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"too